 "notes": "From Fig.3 (Est_d.pdf in e-print), red 95% CL upper-bound curve, extracted as vector path and calibrated from tick strokes (73.19 px/decade in x=log10(m_phi/eV), 28.64 px/decade in y=log10 coupling). Per-mass-bin medians of the noisy observed 95% upper limit. Cross-checks reproduce the papers quoted values: minimum 3.8e-9 at m=1.4e-23 eV, plateau <=5.3e-4 over the whole range, upper mass end 2.4e-18 eV set by omega_max=3.6e-3 rad/s. The plotted curve bounds the linear combination d_e + 0.043(d_mdot - d_g); reported here as the bound on the Damour-Donoghue d_e (the papers phi is dimensionless with alpha(phi)=alpha(1+d_e phi), phi=sqrt(4pi)phi_phys/M_Pl, matching the canonical kappa), which equals this combination when only d_e is nonzero (paper: If only d_e != 0, our limits improve [2] by >1 order of magnitude). DM density assumed rho_DM=0.4 GeV/cm^3 (Eq.8, limit scales as 1/sqrt(rho_DM)); not rescaled.",
